//
// Expected: c1 at one session and at two (GitHub issue #51).
//
// threshold_secret_reveals_no_share.vp with s2 leaked beside k. Alone, k is
// one point of the two-of-three line and fixes no share; with s2 it is two,
// which give away s1. The trace must hand over both before recomposing s1:
// an interpolated share once recorded k as its only ingredient, so the
// trace never mentioned s2 and read as if s1 had been built from k.
attacker[passive]
principal Dealer[
	generates k
	s1, s2, s3 = THRESHOLD_SPLIT[2](k)
	leaks k
	leaks s2
]
Dealer -> Bob: [k]
principal Bob[
	_ = HASH(k)
]
queries[
	confidentiality? s1
]
